Kimochi Manga OCR
Native Rust inference and page grouping for Manga OCR and Comic Text Detector.

Manga OCR: https://github.com/kha-white/manga-ocr (Apache-2.0)
Model: kha-white/manga-ocr-base, revision aa6573bd10b0d446cbf622e29c3e084914df9741
Apache license retained in LICENSE-APACHE.

Comic Text Detector: https://github.com/dmMaze/comic-text-detector (GPL-3.0)
Source revision 440b978563c71b758e31aaa315d100faba1efa2f.
ONNX weights distributed by zyddnys/manga-image-translator, beta-0.2.1.
Pinned asset provenance and checksums: scripts/model-manifest.json.
This combined library is distributed under GPL-3.0-only. Test manga imagery
is not bundled or licensed by this project.

Kimochi also includes MeikiOCR (Apache-2.0), ported from rtr46/meikiocr
revision 52aa607ecdc1038c7bf390f37cd9a8b306e8a08a. Its models and ONNX
Runtime carry their own licenses in the bundled meikiocr resource directory.

Dictionary extensions
Kimochi bundles two browser-extension pop-up dictionaries, each distributed
byte-identical to its upstream release package (unpacked, never modified;
scripts/prepare.mjs verifies every file against extensions/<id>.sha256.json
on each build). The pinned release, asset URL and SHA-256 of each are in
extensions/<id>.source.json. Both are licensed GPL-3.0-or-later and are
distributed here under GPL-3.0, whose text is in LICENSE.

Hachidori: https://github.com/bee-san/hachidori (GPL-3.0-or-later)
Release 0.3.0, commit 51eb85486fd9d9b00561c623bbc6defa60853f16, asset
hachidori-0.3.0-51eb85486fd9-chrome.zip, in extensions/hachidori/. Its
LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and licenses/ directory (notices for
Hoshidicts, Zstandard, zip.js, Emscripten, musl, LLVM runtimes, KANJIDIC2
under CC BY-SA 4.0 and others) are part of that tree; SOURCE.json names the
matching corresponding-source archive and its SHA-256.

10ten Japanese Reader: https://github.com/birchill/10ten-ja-reader
(GPL-3.0-or-later). Release v1.28.0, commit
05e9fe2815de2eb1c7807b3d7bebdef456cbb5d1, asset
10ten-ja-reader-1.28.0-chrome.zip, in extensions/tenten/. The release package
carries no licence file of its own; its GPL text is the one in LICENSE. Its
fonts carry their licences beside them (extensions/tenten/fonts/*.LICENSE.txt).
Its dictionary data (extensions/tenten/data/ and the updates it downloads) is
derived from the JMdict, KANJIDIC and ENAMDICT/JMnedict files of the
Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group
(https://www.edrdg.org/), used in conformance with the Group's licence,
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0.
